# Atelier (v2) — environment template. Copy to .env (gitignored: .env is never committed).
# No secrets in committed files (CLAUDE.md / D-025 / D-026). Fill the blank values in your .env.
#
# Boot order: `npm run db:up` (spawns SurrealDB on loopback + applies all migrations),
# then `npm run dev` (the dashboard). The dashboard mints its OWN per-boot control-plane
# token at startup (see HOOK_TOKEN below) — you do NOT set that here.

# ── Workspace ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Root under which projects are scanned/managed (loopback-only operator machine, D-024).
CODE_ROOT=F:/code

# ── SurrealDB (managed server binary on loopback — D-006/D-007/D-025/D-026c) ───────
# The control plane refuses to boot if SURREAL_WS host is not loopback (D-025).
SURREAL_WS=ws://127.0.0.1:8000
SURREAL_NS=playground
SURREAL_DB=v2
# Runtime user the long-lived dashboard signs in as. In dev this is the root user
# (root/root — the db:up default). In production use a SCOPED least-privilege user
# (D-026c); root is provisioning/migrations only.
SURREAL_USER=root
SURREAL_PASS=root
# Optional (SF2-1 / D-026c): flip the long-lived dashboard to the SCOPED least-priv
# runtime user (`atelier_runtime`, ROLES EDITOR) that `npm run db:up` provisions. Set
# BOTH to the values db:up prints — under these EXACT names; no code edit is required,
# the runtime connect signs in at DATABASE auth level on its own. Once both are set the
# SURREAL_USER/SURREAL_PASS pair above is IGNORED. Leaving BOTH unset keeps the
# historical root path unchanged (additive opt-in). A partial config (one set) is
# rejected with an honest reason — set both or neither.
# SURREAL_RUNTIME_USER=atelier_runtime
# SURREAL_RUNTIME_PASS=<the password db:up printed ONCE for that user>
# Optional: where the surrealkv data lives (gitignored). Defaults to .data
# SURREAL_DATA_DIR=.data
# Optional: separate root provisioning creds for db:up if you split runtime vs root.
# SURREAL_ROOT_USER=root
# SURREAL_ROOT_PASS=root

# ── SvelteKit bind (D-025: loopback ONLY; the boot gate fails closed otherwise) ────
# The Node adapter defaults to 0.0.0.0 — you MUST set HOST=127.0.0.1 in production.
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=5173

# ── Ollama (local model + embeddings — D-003/D-014). NO /v1 suffix. ───────────────
OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# ── Anthropic credential for DRIVEN Claude Code sessions (D-002/S1) ───────────────
# The runtime spawns every session under an ISOLATED CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR carrying ONLY
# this token + the harness gates — never the operator's interactive login. Supply ONE
# (token preferred). LEAVE BLANK here; put the real value in .env only.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Control-plane token (D-025) — MINTED AT BOOT, do NOT set here ─────────────────
# The dashboard mints a fresh per-boot token at startup (hooks.server.ts) and surfaces
# it into its OWN process env as HOOK_TOKEN, plus HOOK_URL for the loopback hook-proxy.
# Leave these UNSET; they are managed by the running server. Only set HOOK_TOKEN here if
# you are running a manual proxy against an already-running server and want a fixed token.
# HOOK_TOKEN=
# HOOK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5173
